{"id":237,"slug":"cries-and-whispers","title":"Cries and Whispers","year":1972,"country":"Sweden","duration":91,"spine":101,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/237-cries-and-whispers","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/8968996394900a7ff0de5a53d03ac392/mCvLwTDCAXEVyMHp4om3piFvSm2nzL_large.jpg","description":"\nThis existential wail of a drama concerns two sisters, Karin (Ingrid Thulin) and Maria (Liv Ullmann), keeping vigil for a third, Agnes (Harriet Andersson), who is dying of cancer and can find solace only in the arms of a beatific servant (Kari Sylwan). An intensely felt film that is one of Bergman’s most striking formal experiments, Cries and Whispers (which won an Oscar for the extraordinary color photography by Sven Nykvist) is a powerful depiction of human behavior in the face of death, positioned on the borders between reality and nightmare, tranquility and terror.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Ingmar Bergman","slug":"ingmar-bergman"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Harriet Andersson","role":"Agnes","slug":"harriet-andersson"},{"actor":"Kari Sylwan","role":"Anna","slug":"kari-sylwan"},{"actor":"Ingrid Thulin","role":"Karin","slug":"ingrid-thulin"},{"actor":"Liv Ullmann","role":"Maria/The mother","slug":"liv-ullmann"},{"actor":"Anders Ek","role":"Pastor Isak","slug":"anders-ek"},{"actor":"Erland Josephson","role":"David","slug":"erland-josephson"},{"actor":"Henning Moritzen","role":"Joakim","slug":"henning-moritzen"},{"actor":"Georg Årlin","role":"Fredrik","slug":"georg-arlin"},{"actor":"Inga Gill","role":"Aunt Olga","slug":"inga-gill"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Ingmar Bergman","slug":"ingmar-bergman"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Ingmar Bergman","slug":"ingmar-bergman"},{"role":"Produced by","person":"Lars-Owe Carlberg","slug":null},{"role":"Director of photography","person":"Sven Nykvist","slug":"sven-nykvist"},{"role":"Art direction","person":"Marik Vos-Lundh","slug":null},{"role":"Sound","person":"Owe Sven